          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The first-person present-tense clause directly avows the speaker's love for Maria. Its oath-like framing in the scene strengthens the assurance that the avowal is true and not a passing fancy.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt end for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"The focal clause presents a current loving state as true; it does not itself undertake an act, obligation, or defined relational commitment. The speaker's adjacent statements about living with Maria carry prospective implications, but their force should not be transferred to this clause.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"Although spoken during an emotional reunion, the expression is a deliberate answer to Maria's doubt and is formulated as a solemn assertion, not as a reflex-like affective outburst.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt end for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"Its core force is adequately represented as an avowal of love under T. The contextual reassurance does not require a distinct residual mode.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"At an emotional reunion, Maria asks whether the speaker's apparent change is genuine, lasting, and not something he will regret the next day. He answers with a solemnly framed declaration that he loves her.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression itself contains no distinct undertaking. In the surrounding turn the speaker separately says that he wants to live a very long time with Maria, but that prospective statement is not assigned to the focal clause. Maria receives the declaration as sincere: she cries because she understands that he is speaking truth and is happy.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognize the work with sufficient certainty from the supplied text.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly supports the represented sincerity and immediate uptake of the avowal, but it does not by itself settle the couple's later conduct or whether any adjacent future-oriented language constitutes a formally accepted commitment.\"}"
